  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_PRINCIPLES_OF_INHERITANCE_AND_VARIATION_DIAGRAM_MCQ_Q01 - Interpretation of monohybrid test cross in pea</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The diagram below represents a genetic cross conducted to determine the unknown genotype of a violet-flowered pea plant showing the dominant phenotype:</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:10px 0;">
<svg width="460" height="260" viewBox="0 0 460 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#ffffff; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">
  <rect x="5" y="5" width="450" height="250" rx="8" fill="#f9fbfd" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <!-- Parents -->
  <rect x="25" y="20" width="170" height="50" rx="6" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="110" y="42" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#5b21b6" text-anchor="middle">Dominant Phenotype</text>
  <text x="110" y="58" font-size="12" fill="#4c1d95" text-anchor="middle">Violet Flower (Genotype: ?)</text>
  
  <text x="215" y="50" font-size="18" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">&times;</text>
  
  <rect x="235" y="20" width="195" height="50" rx="6" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="332" y="42" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">Homozygous Recessive</text>
  <text x="332" y="58" font-size="12" fill="#475569" text-anchor="middle">White Flower (Genotype: ww)</text>
  
  <!-- Arrow down -->
  <line x1="215" y1="75" x2="215" y2="105" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
  <defs>
    <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="6" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M 0 1 L 8 5 L 0 9 z" fill="#334155"/>
    </marker>
  </defs>
  
  <!-- Punnett square box -->
  <g transform="translate(145, 110)">
    <!-- Header cells -->
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="40" height="30" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="20" y="20" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">Gametes</text>
    <rect x="40" y="0" width="60" height="30" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="70" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">w</text>
    <rect x="100" y="0" width="60" height="30" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="130" y="20" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">w</text>
    
    <!-- Row 1 -->
    <rect x="0" y="30" width="40" height="40" fill="#ede9fe" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="20" y="55" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#6d28d9" text-anchor="middle">W</text>
    <rect x="40" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="#f5f3ff" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="70" y="48" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#6d28d9" text-anchor="middle">Ww</text>
    <text x="70" y="63" font-size="10" fill="#7c3aed" text-anchor="middle">Violet</text>
    <rect x="100" y="30" width="60" height="40" fill="#f5f3ff" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="130" y="48" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#6d28d9" text-anchor="middle">Ww</text>
    <text x="130" y="63" font-size="10" fill="#7c3aed" text-anchor="middle">Violet</text>
    
    <!-- Row 2 -->
    <rect x="0" y="70" width="40" height="40" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="20" y="95" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">w</text>
    <rect x="40" y="70" width="60" height="40" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="70" y="88" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">ww</text>
    <text x="70" y="103" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">White</text>
    <rect x="100" y="70" width="60" height="40" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#94a3b8"/>
    <text x="130" y="88" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">ww</text>
    <text x="130" y="103" font-size="10" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">White</text>
  </g>
  
  <!-- Result banner -->
  <rect x="50" y="225" width="360" height="25" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text x="230" y="242" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#92400e" text-anchor="middle">Progeny Ratio: 50% Violet (Ww) and 50% White (ww)</text>
</svg>
</div>
<p>Based on the observed progeny ratio, what is the genotype of the unknown parent flower, and what type of cross is illustrated?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Identification of the Type of Cross</strong><br/>In garden pea plants, crossing an individual showing a dominant phenotype with the homozygous recessive parent (rather than self-crossing) is known as a test cross. It is used to ascertain whether the dominant phenotype is homozygous or heterozygous.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Interpretation of the Progeny Ratio</strong><br/>The test cross yields 50 per cent violet-flowered progeny and 50 per cent white-flowered progeny, giving a characteristic 1:1 ratio. The recessive parent exclusively produces gametes carrying the allele \(w\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Determination of Parental Genotype</strong><br/>For white-flowered progeny (\(ww\)) to appear, the unknown dominant parent must contribute the recessive allele \(w\). Since it also produces violet progeny (\(Ww\)), it must contribute the dominant allele \(W\) in equal proportion. Hence, the unknown dominant parent is heterozygous with genotype \(Ww\).</p>
<p><strong>Final Answer:</strong><br/>The unknown parent plant is heterozygous with genotype \(Ww\), and the cross is a test cross producing a 1:1 phenotypic ratio.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
