  <!-- Parents -->
  <text x="120" y="28" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">Female Parent</text>
  <rect x="70" y="36" width="100" height="28" rx="5" fill="#fce7f3" stroke="#ec4899" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="120" y="55" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#be185d" text-anchor="middle">2n = 32</text>
  
  <text x="320" y="28" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">Male Parent (Drone)</text>
  <rect x="270" y="36" width="100" height="28" rx="5" fill="#e0f2fe" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="320" y="55" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0369a1" text-anchor="middle">n = 16</text>
  
  <!-- Cell divisions labels X and Y -->
  <line x1="120" y1="65" x2="120" y2="105" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#beeArrow)"/>
  <rect x="95" y="75" width="50" height="20" rx="3" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#475569"/>
  <text x="120" y="89" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">[ X ]</text>
  
  <line x1="320" y1="65" x2="320" y2="105" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#beeArrow)"/>
  <rect x="295" y="75" width="50" height="20" rx="3" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#475569"/>
  <text x="320" y="89" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">[ Y ]</text>
  
  <!-- Gametes -->
  <circle cx="85" cy="125" r="18" fill="#fbcfe8" stroke="#db2777"/>
  <text x="85" y="129" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#9d174d" text-anchor="middle">16</text>
  
  <circle cx="155" cy="125" r="18" fill="#fbcfe8" stroke="#db2777"/>
  <text x="155" y="129" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#9d174d" text-anchor="middle">16</text>
  
  <circle cx="320" cy="125" r="18" fill="#bae6fd" stroke="#0284c7"/>
  <text x="320" y="129" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#075985" text-anchor="middle">16</text>
  
  <text x="120" y="155" font-size="11" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Eggs (n = 16)</text>
  <text x="320" y="155" font-size="11" fill="#64748b" text-anchor="middle">Sperm (n = 16)</text>
  
  <!-- Pathway Z (unfertilised egg to male) -->
  <line x1="85" y1="145" x2="85" y2="185" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3,3" marker-end="url(#beeArrow)"/>
  <rect x="50" y="158" width="70" height="18" rx="3" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#d97706"/>
  <text x="85" y="171" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#b45309" text-anchor="middle">[ Z ]</text>
  
  <rect x="40" y="190" width="90" height="30" rx="4" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="85" y="205" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#78350f" text-anchor="middle">Male (Drone)</text>
  <text x="85" y="217" font-size="10" fill="#78350f" text-anchor="middle">n = 16</text>
  
  <!-- Fertilisation to female -->
  <path d="M 155 145 L 155 170 L 255 170 L 255 185" fill="none" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#beeArrow)"/>
  <path d="M 320 145 L 320 170 L 255 170" fill="none" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="238" y="165" font-size="10" font-weight="bold" fill="#047857">Fertilisation</text>
  
  <rect x="210" y="190" width="120" height="30" rx="4" fill="#d1fae5" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <text x="270" y="205" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#064e3b" text-anchor="middle">Female (Queen/Worker)</text>
  <text x="270" y="217" font-size="10" fill="#064e3b" text-anchor="middle">2n = 32</text>
  
  <defs>
    <marker id="beeArrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="6" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M 0 1 L 8 5 L 0 9 z" fill="#475569"/>
    </marker>
  </defs>
</svg>
</div>
<p>Identify the processes labeled <strong>[ X ]</strong>, <strong>[ Y ]</strong>, and <strong>[ Z ]</strong> in the diagram:</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Identification of Process [ X ]</strong><br/>In honey bees, female bees (queens and workers) are diploid with 32 chromosomes (\(2n = 32\)). They form haploid gametes (eggs carrying \(n = 16\) chromosomes) by the reductional cell division known as meiosis.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Identification of Process [ Y ]</strong><br/>Male honey bees (drones) are already haploid, possessing 16 chromosomes (\(n = 16\)). Therefore, to produce viable haploid sperms with 16 chromosomes without reduction, males undergo mitotic cell division (mitosis).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Identification of Process [ Z ]</strong><br/>An unfertilised haploid egg (\(n = 16\)) develops directly into an adult male drone without fusion with a male gamete. This mode of asexual development from an unfertilised ovum is called parthenogenesis.</p>
<p><strong>Final Answer:</strong><br/>Process [ X ] is Meiosis, Process [ Y ] is Mitosis, and Process [ Z ] is Parthenogenesis.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
